{\b\fs32 IniTify (HeatHits) System Features\b0\fs24\par}
{\i For research paper / thesis use\i0\par}
\par
{\b App name:} IniTify\par
{\b Research paper name:} HeatHits\par
{\b Study area:} Tuguegarao City, Cagayan\par
{\b Nature of system:} Decision-support and early-warning system (not a medical diagnostic or treatment device)\par
\par

{\b\fs28 1. System Overview\b0\fs24\par}
\par
IniTify (also referred to in research as HeatHits) is a hybrid artificial intelligence mobile application for heat-risk monitoring, personalized alerts, and emergency assistance during extreme heat conditions. The system combines environmental heat-index data with individual risk factors and classifies heat-related risk into four levels: Low, Moderate, High, and Extreme using a Decision Tree model.\par
\par

{\b\fs28 2. Core Features\b0\fs24\par}
\par

{\b 2.1 Heat-Risk Monitoring\b0\par}
\bullet  Receives and processes heat-index / environmental information for the study area\par
\bullet  Combines heat data with documented individual risk factors: age, health condition, activity level, hydration status, and GPS/location\par
\bullet  Continuously supports monitoring of heat-related health risk based on current conditions\par
\par

{\b 2.2 Personalized Heat-Risk Assessment (Decision Tree)\b0\par}
\bullet  Uses a Decision Tree classifier to assess heat risk\par
\bullet  Outputs one of four risk levels: Low, Moderate, High, Extreme\par
\bullet  Integrates environmental heat index with user profile factors\par
\bullet  Displays assessment results and related guidance in the application\par
\par

{\b 2.3 Personalized Recommendations\b0\par}
\bullet  Provides precautionary guidance based on heat risk, such as:\par
\tab - Hydration reminders\par
\tab - Rest and recovery\par
\tab - Seeking shade\par
\tab - Limiting outdoor activities\par
\par

{\b 2.4 Heat-Risk Alerts and Notifications\b0\par}
\bullet  Notifies the user when heat risk requires attention\par
\bullet  Communicates current heat-risk level and recommended precautions\par
\bullet  Supports local notifications (with user permission)\par
\bullet  Designed to require explicit user acknowledgment (not merely opening a notification)\par
\par

{\b 2.5 Safety Prompts and User Acknowledgment\b0\par}
\bullet  Allows the user to respond to safety prompts (e.g., \ldblquote I\rquote m OK\rdblquote  / \ldblquote Need help\rdblquote )\par
\bullet  Records user responses for monitoring and escalation logic\par
\bullet  Supports the research concept that repeated failure to respond may indicate a heat-related emergency\par
\par

{\b 2.6 Multi-Condition Emergency Escalation\b0\par}
\bullet  Emergency assistance does not activate based on a single missed alert alone\par
\bullet  Uses a multi-condition approach to reduce false alarms\par
\bullet  Documented possible indicators include:\par
\tab 1. Extreme heat-risk level\par
\tab 2. Repeated failure to respond to safety prompts\par
\tab 3. Prolonged inactivity at the same location\par
\bullet  Escalation is designed to activate when multiple indicators are present\par
\par

{\b 2.7 Emergency Contact Notification\b0\par}
\bullet  When emergency conditions are satisfied, the system prepares notification content for the designated emergency contact\par
\bullet  Payload may include:\par
\tab - User name\par
\tab - Current heat-risk level\par
\tab - Last known location\par
\tab - Nearest hospital / health facility\par
\tab - Estimated travel time\par
\par

{\b 2.8 Emergency Assistance Screen\b0\par}
\bullet  Displays emergency status and related assistance information\par
\bullet  Shows emergency contact details (when configured)\par
\bullet  Provides access to nearest hospital and navigation\par
\bullet  Presents basic first-aid / heat-stroke guidance\par
\bullet  Supports safety check-in actions during potential emergencies\par
\par

{\b 2.9 Nearest Hospital and Navigation\b0\par}
\bullet  Identifies nearby hospitals/facilities using GPS and a local hospital reference list for Tuguegarao\par
\bullet  Opens maps/navigation directions to the selected facility\par
\bullet  Can be offered during check-in when the user\rquote s situation indicates elevated danger\par
\par

{\b 2.10 AI Check-In Assistant (Tify)\b0\par}
\bullet  Provides a conversational check-in experience with the AI character Tify\par
\bullet  Collects hydration status, activity level, and how the user feels in the heat\par
\bullet  Offers situational heat-safety guidance\par
\bullet  Supports saving check-in records and viewing check-in history\par
\bullet  May present a nearest-hospital call-to-action when appropriate\par
\par

{\b 2.11 Live Weather and Heat Index Display\b0\par}
\bullet  Displays current weather conditions for Tuguegarao City\par
\bullet  Shows temperature, humidity, heat index, and related weather details\par
\bullet  Supports automatic weather refresh (e.g., every 15 minutes) with countdown feedback\par
\bullet  Aligns heat-index values used in guidance with live environmental data\par
\par

{\b 2.12 User Profile and Health Vulnerability Setup\b0\par}
\bullet  Captures user identity and risk-related profile data\par
\bullet  Records age, health conditions, activity level, and hydration-related status\par
\bullet  Stores emergency contact information for escalation use\par
\bullet  Supports health profile updates after initial setup\par
\par

{\b 2.13 Authentication and Account Management\b0\par}
\bullet  Supports user sign-up and login\par
\bullet  Links profile and app data to authenticated users (when cloud auth is configured)\par
\par

{\b 2.14 Notifications and Reminders\b0\par}
\bullet  In-app notification center for alerts and updates\par
\bullet  Check-in reminder settings to encourage regular heat-safety check-ins\par
\par

{\b 2.15 Safety Tips and Health Knowledge Support\b0\par}
\bullet  Provides preventive heat-safety tips and guidance\par
\bullet  Complements emergency first-aid content with educational safety information\par
\par

{\b 2.16 Offline Support\b0\par}
\bullet  Caches important heat and assessment-related information for limited-connectivity situations\par
\bullet  Allows continued access to key stored data when offline\par
\par

{\b 2.17 Location Services\b0\par}
\bullet  Uses GPS for hospital lookup, emergency assistance, and location logging\par
\bullet  Weather/heat monitoring for the study uses fixed Tuguegarao study-area coordinates\par
\par

{\b\fs28 3. Main Application Modules\b0\fs24\par}
\par
{\b Home} \endash  Overview of current heat/risk status and quick access to key features\par
{\b Weather} \endash  Live weather and heat-index information for Tuguegarao\par
{\b Check-in (Tify)} \endash  AI-assisted conversational heat check-in\par
{\b Notifications} \endash  Alerts, reminders, and in-app messages\par
{\b Emergency} \endash  Safety prompts, emergency status, first-aid, hospital/contact actions\par
{\b Profile} \endash  Account, health profile, and settings\par
{\b Assessment / Recommendations} \endash  Decision Tree risk result and precautionary advice\par
{\b Hospital} \endash  Nearest facility and navigation support\par
{\b Offline} \endash  Cached heat and assessment information\par
\par

{\b\fs28 4. Technical Capabilities\b0\fs24\par}
\par
\bullet  Cross-platform mobile application (Expo / React Native)\par
\bullet  Live environmental data integration for Tuguegarao (Open-Meteo)\par
\bullet  Heat index computation from temperature and humidity\par
\bullet  Decision Tree risk classification engine\par
\bullet  Local device storage with optional cloud database synchronization (Supabase / MySQL)\par
\bullet  Local notifications and reminder scheduling\par
\bullet  GPS-based hospital and emergency location support\par
\bullet  Offline caching for critical information\par
\par

{\b\fs28 5. Data Management Features\b0\fs24\par}
\par
The system can store and/or sync records related to:\par
\bullet  Users and risk profiles\par
\bullet  Emergency contacts\par
\bullet  Heat-index readings and weather refresh logs\par
\bullet  Risk assessments\par
\bullet  Recommendation logs\par
\bullet  Heat-alert logs\par
\bullet  Safety-prompt responses\par
\bullet  Emergency events and contact notifications\par
\bullet  Hospital lookups and location logs\par
\bullet  Check-in records\par
\bullet  Offline cache snapshots\par
\par

{\b\fs28 6. Safety and Ethical Positioning\b0\fs24\par}
\par
\bullet  IniTify is a decision-support and early-warning system.\par
\bullet  It is not a medical diagnostic device and does not replace professional medical care.\par
\bullet  Multi-condition emergency escalation is used to reduce false alarms.\par
\bullet  Users in danger should seek appropriate emergency services and medical facilities.\par
\par

{\b\fs28 7. Sample Paragraph for Papers\b0\fs24\par}
\par
IniTify (HeatHits) is a mobile heat-risk monitoring and emergency-assistance system designed for Tuguegarao City, Cagayan. It integrates real-time environmental heat-index data with individual factors\emdash age, health condition, activity level, and hydration\emdash to classify heat-related risk into Low, Moderate, High, or Extreme using a Decision Tree. The application provides personalized recommendations, safety prompts, and notifications, and supports multi-condition emergency escalation to reduce false alarms. Additional features include AI-assisted check-ins, nearest-hospital guidance, offline caching, and emergency first-aid information. The system functions as a decision-support and early-warning tool and is not intended as a medical diagnostic device.\par
\par

{\b\fs28 8. Suggested Limitations (Optional Section)\b0\fs24\par}
\par
\bullet  Some emergency threshold values (response timeout, number of failed prompts, inactivity duration) may remain configurable pending final research approval.\par
\bullet  Production SMS or call delivery to emergency contacts depends on external service configuration.\par
\bullet  Weather used for heat-risk monitoring is based on the Tuguegarao study area; GPS is primarily used for hospital and emergency features.\par
\bullet  AI check-in guidance is advisory and does not constitute a medical diagnosis.\par
\par
